Changes made for this project:

- SKILL.md is rewritten in Japanese for business documents and for the markdown_create tool
  of Production Ready Agent. Only the guidance that applies to a single Markdown file made
  by that tool is kept: one title heading, heading levels without skips and with
  descriptive text, blank lines around blocks, list markers and the indentation of nested
  items, sparing emphasis, tables with a header row and a delimiter row and right-aligned
  number columns, fenced code blocks with a language name, descriptive link text,
  footnotes for sources, task lists, Mermaid diagrams for structure (choosing the diagram
  type by content, a sentence that describes each diagram, splitting large diagrams) and
  tables instead of Mermaid for quantitative values.
- Added for this project: emphasis delimiters are kept away from Japanese brackets and
  punctuation (CommonMark flanking rules), no front matter unless asked for, no raw HTML,
  no diagram types whose names end in "-beta", and the size of a table and the use of the
  other file tools (Excel, Word, PowerPoint) for large tables and charts.
- Removed: emoji in headings and in diagram nodes, the approved emoji set, horizontal
  rules after collapsible sections, collapsible HTML sections, the document templates,
  the per-diagram reference files, colors and classDef styling, accessibility directives
  of Mermaid, images and figure files, rendering and validating diagrams with the Mermaid
  CLI or a browser, version control of the sources, and the integration with other
  scientific skills.

